-- title:
--   Polynomial space bound for the selected-color pipeline
-- statement:
--   For natural numbers $f,n,U$, let $\operatorname{space}_{\mathrm{pipeline}}(f,n,U)$ be the largest address required by the closed selected-color construction starting at free address $f$. Its aggregate scale is
--   $$\sigma(n)=M_{\mathrm{report}}(n)+E_{\mathrm{local}}(n)+M_{\max}(n)+P_{\mathrm{window}}(n)+n+100,$$
--   where the terms are the defined reporting-bank magnitude, local-cover envelope, maximum modulus, and prime-window bound. Then
--   $$\operatorname{space}_{\mathrm{pipeline}}(f,n,U)\le f+3000\sigma(n)^5+U.$$
--   The statement holds for every natural input size and value bound.
--
--   This supplies an allocation bound that adds the already occupied prefix only once and can be used when composing the pipeline with later reporting stages.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorPipelineResources.lean#L13-L29

